# ── Local secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# If you ever run scan.mjs/backtest.mjs locally with
# `node --env-file=.env scripts/scan.mjs`, put TWELVEDATA_API_KEY in
# .env — never commit that file. .env.example (committed) is the template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ── OS / editor cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ── Node (only matters if you add npm dependencies later —
#    scan.mjs/backtest.mjs currently use zero external packages) ──
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ── Local scratch/test runs ────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment if you want to experiment with scan.mjs/backtest.mjs locally
# without touching the "real" committed history the live site reads from.
# Leave these OUT of .gitignore for the deployed repo — data/latest.json
# and data/history* are supposed to be committed; that's how the Auto Scan
# tab gets its data with zero API calls per visit.
# data/latest.json
# data/history.jsonl
# data/history/
